.TH cpp_tokenize_file 3
.SH NAME
cpp_tokenize_file \- read and tokenize a source file
.SH SYNTAX
.B #include "cpp.h"

cpp_token* \fBcpp_tokenize_file\fP(cpp_ctx* \fIpp\fR, char* \fIpath\fR);
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBcpp_tokenize_file\fP reads the file at \fIpath\fR, normalizes newlines, strips backslash-newline continuations, converts universal character names, registers the file in context \fIpp\fR, and tokenizes its contents.

Returns a pointer to the head of the token list on success, or NULL if the file cannot be read.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
cpp_tokenize(3), cpp_preprocess(3)